==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an Indo-European root ''*skai-, *ski-''.  Cognate with Old High German ''skīnan'' (German ''[[scheinen]]''), Old Saxon ''skīnan'' (Dutch ''[[schijnen]]''), Old Norse ''[[skína]]'' (Swedish ''[[skina]]''), Gothic [[𐍃𐌺𐌴𐌹𐌽𐌰𐌽]].  The IE root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{term|lang=grc|σκιά}}, Old Slavic ''sěn’'' (Russian ''[[сень]]'').

